      "Method overview. Capture link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Compare a documented baseline with scheduled link verification at intake, decision handoff, and closure. The field dictionary, inclusion rules, sampling method, and analysis code are frozen before outcomes are examined.",
      "Field audit. Before analysis, independently trace each required field for evidence-link decay back to the source that created it and the system event that last changed it. Mark whether the value is observed, derived, owner-supplied, or reviewer-coded. Retain nulls and conflicts; do not convert absence into a negative result. Reconcile extracted records to source control totals and explain exclusions by reason. Reperform a subset from the original systems using the frozen dictionary, compare the second result with the first, and preserve disagreement before adjudication. This audit distinguishes a workflow finding from an extraction defect and makes the eventual denominator reviewable. Record the extractor, query or export version, execution time, time-zone conversion, and checksum so a later reviewer can determine whether a changed result came from the workflow or the evidence pipeline.",
