      "Define the unit. Give each included observation one stable key and a clear entry and exit event. Separate a queue item, human action, owner decision, and destination event rather than counting them as interchangeable work. For evidence-link decay, stage 2 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Build the evidence map. Preserve source facts, assistant preparation, owner decisions, execution, and verification in separate fields. Record unavailable evidence instead of replacing it with an inference. For evidence-link decay, stage 3 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Control access and retention. Use synthetic cases first, then purpose-limited operational samples only with approved access. Keep sensitive source records in their governed systems and remove temporary study permissions. For evidence-link decay, stage 4 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Freeze the baseline. Observe comparable cycles before changing the workflow. Record volume, exception mix, owner availability, outages, policy changes, and seasonal events that could explain a result. For evidence-link decay, stage 5 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Apply one intervention. Introduce the specified control without simultaneously changing staffing, tools, definitions, and deadlines. Log unavoidable changes as limitations rather than attributing every difference to the intervention. For evidence-link decay, stage 6 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Review independently. Have trained reviewers classify selected observations before discussion. Preserve disagreement, confidence, unavailable records, and the reason a final disposition changed. For evidence-link decay, stage 7 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Sample representatively. Include every predefined high-consequence exception and a reproducible random sample of ordinary work. Document substitutions so easy cases cannot silently replace unavailable records. For evidence-link decay, stage 8 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Measure without hiding risk. Report counts with denominators, medians, ranges, age bands, corrections, rework, and unresolved cases. Do not let numerous low-risk completions offset one unauthorized or harmful action. For evidence-link decay, stage 9 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Test sensitivity. Repeat calculations under plausible cutoff, missing-evidence, pause-time, risk-band, and unresolved-case treatments. Identify conclusions that depend on policy choices. For evidence-link decay, stage 10 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
      "Trace corrective action. Link each finding to an owner, due date, implementation reference, verification result, and residual limitation. A meeting or revised instruction is not proof that operating state changed. For evidence-link decay, stage 11 must preserve link target, permission state, source version, observation time, failure type, recovery route, and owner. Reviewers distinguish what the system recorded from what the business concluded and retain alternative explanations when evidence conflicts.",
